# fig_diagnostic

**Claim carried:** C3/E8: a labels-only diagnostic predicts whether calibration will shorten the interval.

**Shows:** per (dataset, n, calibrator) cell: relative width gain predicted from the cross-fitted gap minus learning cost (x) against realised gain (1 - paired width ratio to PPI++, y, 95% CI); dashed line = identity; axes follow the points, so a CI longer than the axis is cut at its edge. Real sets: reference grid and the monotone-transformed outcomes; synthetic: E1 sweeps.

**How to read:** points on the dashed line: the diagnostic predicts the size of the gain; same quadrant: it gets the sign right (share in tables/fig5_stats.json). Cells with no diagnostic value are not drawn; their count is n_cells - n_drawn in that file.

